{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]I'm going fishing, Peter said
And [F]we went with him [C]too
All night we fished on Galilee
And [G]not a fish came through
[C]At dawn a man stood on the shore
[F]Have you any [C]fish, my friends
Cast the net on the right [G]side
And you will [C]find some then
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Cast the net on the [F]right side
[C]Haul it in, haul it in
A hundred fifty three great [G]fish
And the [C]net [C]was not torn
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
It is the Lord, said John [F]to him
And Peter jumped [C]into the sea
A fire of coals upon [G]the beach
With fish and [C]bread for free
Come and have breakfast, Je[F]sus said
And no one [C]dared to ask
They knew it was the Lord him[G]self
Who served them [C]at the last
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Cast the net on [F]the right side
[C]Haul it in, haul it [G]in [C][F][C][G][C][F][C][G][C][F]
[C]A hundred fifty three great fish
And the [G]net was not [C]torn
{end_of_chorus}
